 "title": "About IIMB | IIM Bangalore",
 "text": "About IIMB\nOverview\n\nThe Indian Institute of Management Bangalore (IIMB) is a leading graduate school of management in Asia. Under the IIM Act of 2017, IIMB is an Institute of National Importance.\n\nIIMB has 105 full-time faculty members, about 1,200 students across various degree-granting programmes and nearly 5,000 annual Executive Education participants.\n\nOur logo carries a proclamation in Sanskrit, तेजस्वि नावधीतमस्तु (tejasvi navadhitamastu), which translates to ‘let our study be enlightening’. Our vision is to be a global, renowned academic institution fostering excellence in management, innovation and entrepreneurship for business, government and society.\n\nRead more...\n\nOur Vision\nMotto\nVision\nMission\nValues\nGuiding Principles\nInspiration, Excellence, Achievement\n\nIIMB has a strong brand identity with a logo that has great recall. The sun symbol has been designed by the National Institute of Design, Ahmedabad, and has been in use since 1994.\n\nThe concept of the current logo is based on a line from the Sanskrit shloka which has become the motto of IIMB: Tejasvi navadhitamastu. This line, derived from the peace invocation of several Upanishads, translates as: “Let our study be enlightening”.\n\n \n\nLet us together be protected and let us together be nourished by God’s blessings / Let us together join our mental forces in strength for the benefit of humanity / Let our study be enlightening / Let us never be poisoned with the seeds of hatred for anyone / Let there be peace and serenity in all the three universes.\n\n- Invocation from Taittiriya Upanishad\n\nArchitecture\n\nIIMB Sustainability Report\n\nIIMB Sustainability Report 2025\n\nCarbon Footprint Report 2025\n\nAccreditation and Rankings\n\nInternational Accreditation\n\nIIMB has been internationally accredited by the EFMD Quality Improvement System (EQUIS) since 2010. In December 2021, IIMB was re-accredited by EQUIS for a further period of five years.\n\nThe EFMD Quality Improvement System is a leading international system of quality assessment, improvement and accreditation of business schools, run by the European Foundation for Management Development (EFMD). EQUIS has accredited some 202 institutions in 45 countries around the world. EQUIS accreditation ensures a rigorous quality control and benchmarking of a business school against international standards in terms of governance, programmes, students, faculty, research, internationalisation, ethics, responsibility and sustainability, as well as engagement with the world of practice.\n\nThe five-year accreditation, the highest that EQUIS confers, is a testimony to the fact that the evaluating team was confident of IIMB’s ability to sustain its efforts undertaken to achieve international standards of excellence in research and management education.\n\nBoard\nChairperson\nDr. Devi Prasad Shetty\n\nChairman and Founder Narayana Health\n\nchair[at]iimb[dot]ac[dot]in\n\nMessage from Chairperson\n\nDirector-in-charge\nU Dinesh Kumar\n\ndirector[at]iimb[dot]ac[dot]in\n\nSl.No\tName\tDesignation\n1.\tDr. Devi Prasad Shetty\tChairperson, Board of Governors, IIMB\nChairman and Founder Narayana Health\n2.\tDr. Hasmukh Adhia\tFormer Finance Secretary, Government of India\n3.\tMr. Sonjoy Chatterjee\tChairman & CEO  Goldman Sachs (India) Securities Pvt Ltd.\n4.\tProfessor Jitamitra Desai\tProfessor, IIMB\n5.\tProfessor U Dinesh Kumar\tDirector-in-charge, IIMB\n6.\tMs. Shanti Ekambaram\tDirector, Kotak Mahindra Capital Company and Director Kotak Securities Limited\n7.\tMs. Malavika R Harita\tFounder & CEO, Brand Circle and Former CEO Saatchi Focus India\n8.\tProfessor Sreelata Jonnalagedda\tProfessor, IIMB\n9.\tProfessor Das Narayandas\tEdsel Bryant Ford Professor of Business Administration at the Harvard Business School, Boston, USA\n10.\tDr. Shalini Rajneesh, IAS\tChief Secretary, Government of Karnataka\n11.\tMr. M. D. Ranganath\tChairman, Catamaran Ventures\n12.\tMs. Kalpana Saroj\tChairperson, Kamani Tubes\n13.\tDr. K M Praphullachandra Sharma\tJoint Secretary (International Cooperation & Management)\n14.\tProfessor Raji Srinivasan\tJack R. Crosby Regents Chair in Business Administration at the Red McCombs School of Business,  University of Texas at Austin, USA\n \tSpecial Invitees\n \tProfessor Venkatesh Panchapagesan\tDean (Administration), IIMB\n \tProfessor Mukta Kulkarni\tDean (Programmes), IIMB\n \tProfessor Sourav Mukherji\tDean (Faculty), IIMB\n \tProfessor Vasanthi Srinivasan\tDean (Alumni Relations and Development), IIMB\n \t\n\nThe Board, was originally constituted on March 27 1972, and last updated on 14 August, 2026.\n\n* Listed in alphabetical order of last names.\n\nIIM Act and Rules\n\nIndian Institutes of Management Act, 2017\n\nIndian Institutes of Management Act Amendment 2023\n\nIndian Institutes of Management Rules, 2018\n\nIndian Institutes of Management Rules Amendment 2023\n\nOrganisational Structure\n\nView The Structure\n\nInternational Advisory Committee\nProfessor\nRuth Aguilera,\n\nDarla and Frederick Brodsky Trustee Professor in Global Business; Distinguished Professor, International Business and Strategy, Northeastern University\n\nProfessor\nBharat Anand,\n\nRichard R. West Dean of NYU Stern and Professor of Business Administration\n\nProfessor\nDavid Bach,\n\nPresident of IMD and Nestlé Professor of Strategy and Political Economy\n\nProfessor\nGerry George,\n\nTamsen and Michael Brown Family Professor of Entrepreneurship and Innovation and Academic Advisor to the Georgetown Entrepreneurship Initiative\n\nProfessor\nKrishna Rajagopal,\n\nWilliam A. M. Burden Professor of Physics Margaret MacVicar Faculty Fellow\n\nProfessor\nRaghu Sundaram,\n\nSenior Vice Chancellor and Chief Global Officer, New York University\nDean Emeritus, NYU Stern Edward I. Altman Professor of Credit and Debt Markets\nProfessor of Finance\n\nProfessor\nLin Zhou,\n\nDean of The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) Business School and Choh-Ming Li\nProfessor of Economics\n\n* Last updated on August 14, 2026.\n* Listed in alphabetical order of last names.\n\n ",
